--- MAME (BSD-3-Clause) --------------------------------------------------------

This emulator's hardware model was reconstructed from MAME source files
marked `license:BSD-3-Clause`. The code is a JavaScript reimplementation, not
a copy, but the algorithms, constant tables, and register layouts come from
those files — some tables (e.g. the PCD3311 tone frequencies) were copied
over directly. The notices below fall under the same license text as the one
given above.

Copyright (c) Curt Coder
    src/mame/atari/pofo.cpp
    src/devices/video/hd61830.cpp, hd61830.h
    src/devices/sound/pcd3311.cpp, pcd3311.h
    src/devices/bus/pofo/ccm.cpp, exp.cpp, hpc101.cpp, hpc102.cpp, hpc104.cpp

Copyright (c) Curt Coder, Jaen Saul
    src/mame/atari/pofo_kbd.cpp

Copyright (c) smf, Carl
    src/devices/machine/ins8250.cpp, ins8250.h

These files' headers give the rights holders without stating years. The MAME
project as a whole carries the notice `Copyright (c) 1997-2026 MAMEDev and
contributors`. Project site: https://www.mamedev.org/

--- MartyPC (MIT) ---------------------------------------------------------------

The CPU core, js/emu/cpu8088.js, and its decode table, js/emu/cpu8088-decode.js,
are a JavaScript port of the 808x core of MartyPC
(https://github.com/dbalsom/martypc, crates/lib/marty_core/src/cpu_808x), made
function for function; the decode table was generated from its decode.rs.

Copyright 2022-2026 Daniel Balsom

